#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:5
#: 66ae13ed09e34127af908c05fe6e7690
msgid "Blue Robotics Ping Underwater Sonar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:7
#: e79c483f4c364ccfb559cd9b3e2f7802
msgid "The `Blue Robotics Underwater Sonar <https://bluerobotics.com/store/sensors-sonars-cameras/sonar/ping-sonar-r2-rp/>`__ is a single-beam encosounder with a maximum range of 100m, a beam width of 25deg and a maximum depth rating of 300m.  More details can be found in the `Technical Details section of the product page on Blue Robotics <https://bluerobotics.com/store/sensors-sonars-cameras/sonar/ping-sonar-r2-rp/#tab-technical-details>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:11
#: 4daf4a80fe5d4826a6154222bf50aa1a
msgid "Rover-4.1.0 (and higher) require the Ping sensor be running firmware version 3.28 (or higher).  See below for how to upgrade the Ping's firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:14
#: 4fa0e0b050524d03bf464aa4f2195735
msgid "Where to Buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:16
#: c76125919f14487b9c0e95e659d3ee88
msgid "This sensor can be purchased directly from `Blue Robotics <https://bluerobotics.com/store/sensors-sonars-cameras/sonar/ping-sonar-r2-rp/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:17
#: f6dce02ce95c433891a2d3eda1189534
msgid "Optionally the `BLUART USB to Serial RS485 adapter <https://bluerobotics.com/store/comm-control-power/tether-interface/bluart-r1-rp/>`__ allows connecting the sensor to a PC for testing, or to a Companion computer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:20
#: 289bc8d48ef347e6a531ce29770f4448
msgid "Connecting to the Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:22
#: 3dbc68a0ed0448359964412d6665c76e
msgid "For a serial connection you can use any spare Serial/UART port.  The diagram below shows how to connect to SERIAL2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:27
#: 1b0f146a79044f18a034e1ac4b9df46d
msgid "If the SERIAL2 port on the autopilot is being used then the following parameters should be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:29
#: effc04b1256f418a93c7bb5346e8373f
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 9 (Lidar)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:30
#: c7e1ef2313204e7ea046ba61146f8f10
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <SERIAL2_BAUD>` = 115 (115200 baud)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:31
#: 314deda34dcb425f964a713c6e48fe48
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE <RNGFND1_TYPE>` = 23 (BlueRoboticsPing)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:32
#: 17dc010b09d74feb84ed2aeb4e464aa0
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MIN <RNGFND1_MIN>` = 0.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:33
#: bc07da85851d47598e2ec145943aea40
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MAX <RNGFND1_MAX>` = 96.  This is the distance in meters that the rangefinder can reliably read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:34
#: 1dae046b479447778158fc44fa067dac
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_ORIENT <RNGFND1_ORIENT>` = 25 (down) if mounted on a boat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:37
#: 8758de42b7644f8da9e58692772b749d
msgid "PingViewer to test and upgrade the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:39
#: f1583cb53ac748a796b3b6f63861f017
msgid "`BlueRobotic's PingViewer <https://docs.bluerobotics.com/ping-viewer/>`__ can be used to test the sensor and `upgrade the firmware <https://docs.bluerobotics.com/ping-viewer/firmware-update/>`__. There is `an open source sonar firmware <https://github.com/bluerobotics/ping-firmware-oss>`__ which can be used to test modified signal processing and rangefinding algorithms, or create fully custom behaviors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:41
#: 6f08b1dd755d4791b81fc824c125a350
msgid "Connect the Ping to your PC using a USB cable and `BLUART USB to Serial RS485 adapter <https://bluerobotics.com/store/comm-control-power/tether-interface/bluart-r1-rp/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:42
#: 54d85efbd864408cb958172e45787a70
msgid "Download, install and run the PingViewer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:43
#: fdf7a02511ac4c56b28b13554d442fd7
msgid "From within the PingViewer application connect to the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:44
#: e1de7aead7a241028dfc0bd5fab2e7a1
msgid "From the upper left menu, select the gear icon, `Firmware Upgrade <https://docs.bluerobotics.com/ping-viewer/firmware-update/>`__ and if necessary upgrade the firmware to \"Ping_V3.28_auto\" (or higher), or install a custom firmware binary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-bluerobotics-ping.rst:51
#: 0e88f6dd91b64cbb89aabd2c3a03bbb9
msgid "Testing the sensor"
msgstr ""

